# Review of the closure glue (hunt HSTR2-01): each mode at 1000 and 4000
# (RtIOFinishAlloc.lean). Natively a `putStr` to a handle makes 1
# allocation (its result) and a `getLine` 3; lean2rr's glue built two
# closures at every call (3 and 6 allocations).
put 1000 | put 4000 | 1 200
line 1000 | line 4000 | 1 200
out 1000 | out 4000 | 1 200
# Hunt HIOG2. A failing `putStr` (an error without a file name): natively 3
# allocations (the details, the IO.Error, the result), lean2rr 5 (the
# runtime's IoError holds its own copy of the details and the last-error
# slot one more; before, the glue also read the file name: 6). The bound
# keeps the error path within twice native's.
fail 1000 | fail 4000 | 2 200
# `getEnv` (per call of these loops): natively 2 allocations for a set
# variable and none for an unset one; lean2rr 3 (lean-runtime's lookup
# copies the value once more) and none. Before, a `some` closure at every
# call and a second lookup for the value: 6 and 1.
envset 1000 | envset 4000 | 2 200
envunset 1000 | envunset 4000 | 1 200
